From: LuneOS <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sdm670: label the pshold restart node msm_poweroff

Every one of the ten device tree overlays in a Pixel 3a's stock Android 11
dtbo partition references the symbol "msm_poweroff". This tree declares the
node but gives it no label, so it never reaches __symbols__ and the overlay's
phandle cannot be resolved. The bootloader gives up before starting the
kernel:

    Booting  FAILED (remote: 'Error verifying the received boot.img:
                              Invalid Parameter')
    Error boot prepare

which is what a LuneOS boot image did on a Pixel 3a after flashing stock
Android 11, while an otherwise identical image carrying Google's own device
tree booted. Comparing __symbols__ between the two trees showed four
differences, and msm_poweroff was the only one the dtbo actually references.

Google's own sdm670.dtsi labels this node; this restores the label so the
stock overlays apply against a kernel built from these sources. It costs one
symbol table entry and changes nothing else.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device tree matches a vendor blob]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm670.dtsi
@@ -1005,7 +1005,7 @@
 		};
 	};
 
-	restart@10ac000 {
+	msm_poweroff: restart@10ac000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,pshold";
 		reg = <0xC264000 0x4>,
 		      <0x1fd3000 0x4>;
